  Confirm the fix                                                               
  Subject: ~/.ssh has mode 0755.                                                
  Scope: one deterministic change; nothing else on the machine is touched.      
  Effect: before: /home/testuser/.ssh has mode 0755.                            
  Effect: after:  /home/testuser/.ssh has mode 0700.                            
  Risk: A mode that is too open is a way into every tool that reads this path,  
  and OpenSSH refuses to use a key inside a directory others can read.          
  Permission: Ownership of /home/testuser/.ssh; no administrator rights are     
  needed when this user owns it.                                                
  Backup: The mode it has now (0755) is written into the fix record with the    
  command that puts it back: `chmod 0755 /home/testuser/.ssh`.                  
  Apply: [a] applies it.                                                        
  Leave: Escape leaves without changing anything.                               
                                                                                
  ▸ [a] Set the mode to 0700                                                    
